      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`send_weights_to_remote_instance()` indexes `_weights_send_group` before its missing-group branch. Sending before initialization, or sending again after the first call consumes the group, therefore raises `KeyError` instead of returning the existing initialization guidance.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nUse `dict.get()` for the guard. Existing `None` handling, broadcasts and process-group cleanup are unchanged. Add three registered CPU regression tests covering unknown groups, `None` groups, and a successful send followed by a repeated call (including TP rank/port selection).\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Real module imports and single-rank CPU Gloo A/B, Python 3.12 / Torch 2.11.0+cu130: all four candidate checks passed (missing, None, successful broadcast, repeat-after-send). The unchanged baseline raised `KeyError` in the missing/repeated cases. No GPU, server or model download was used.\r\n- Applicable pre-commit formatting/lint checks passed. Three local hooks required invoking their unchanged scripts with `python` because Windows has no working `python3` launcher; all three then passed.\r\n- The unchanged registered `test/registered/unit/model_executor/model_runner_components/test_weight_exporter.py` now runs against complete package source with no import stubs: candidate `aa2a943` passes 3/3; the unchanged production control errors in the missing/repeated cases and passes the `None` control. Linux / Python 3.12 / Torch 2.11.0+cu130, CPU engine, no install or model download.\r\n- CUDA remained uninitialized. The framework parses the first character of `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, so the local CPU run used absent ordinal `9` after verifying physical indices 0–7. Both arms emitted the same optional CUDA-backend probe warnings under the process memory bound. This is a local registered-test result, not official CI; `base-a-test-cpu` still requires maintainer authorization.\r\n\r\nModel-output accuracy and speed benchmarks are not applicable to this error-path fix.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted implementation and investigation.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38600672418](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38600672418)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38600672456](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38600672456)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38600672562](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38600672562)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
